Looks syntactically fine. One issue: `requestActor` reads `body.actorId` where body could be null if JSON `null` parsed. `readJson` returns null for "null". Then `requestActor(req,url,null)` default only applies undefined, so body.actorId throws TypeError -> 500. Existing code also would throw on body.title for null. Not our concern, but could harden. Maybe not.

Another issue: `shareTargetFrom(body)` if body null -> TypeError. Existing validation would also. Fine.

Another issue: For `POST /todos/:id/share`, if body has `actorId` and `sharedWith`, fine.

Another issue: `GET /todos?viewerId=` empty string -> treated false, falls to owner filter. Fine.

